  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116004",
      "title": "Using The Alternative Dependency Injection Syntax",
      "lectureOrder": 180,
      "videoOrder": 172,
      "sourceHash": "ddedb06df2f66a2941f5570dc96c7aadec34ba7ebef3751df2826d14f0813d88",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3,
          "en": "So here in the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "we of course also want to use that tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "because it's here where we need to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 10.593,
          "en": "output the tasks in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.49,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "So therefore, we also want to inject the tasks service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 16.77,
          "en": "into the tasks list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.77,
          "end": 18.87,
          "en": "We could do this with the constructor again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "that would be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "And there are Angular developers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 23.94,
          "en": "who always use this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "because they prefer it, which is of course fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.12,
          "en": "But there also is an alternative syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.12,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "Instead of using the constructor, you can add a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "a private or a non-private, a public one, it doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "Here, I'll go for a private one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 42.003,
          "en": "which I'll also name tasks service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 46.08,
          "en": "And then you can assign an injected value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.08,
          "end": 46.924,
          "en": "and request such a value from Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.924,
          "end": 51.924,
          "en": "with help of the built-in inject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.76,
          "end": 56.133,
          "en": "which is imported from Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "This inject function can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 63.13,
          "en": "to request a dependency from Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.05,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "and to inject you then pass your injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "as it's called, which in the end is again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.833,
          "en": "the service class name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "So again, just as before, you must import tasks service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 83.34,
          "en": "into the tasks list component, and then use that class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 85.113,
          "en": "as a value for inject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "With that, the service is available here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "And now, we can replace the dummy tasks array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 97.65299999999999,
          "en": "which is always empty with the tasks from our service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "For that, we can use the tasks service like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 105.27000000000001,
          "en": "and then refer to tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.27000000000001,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "And tasks is then a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.363,
          "en": "So now, tasks here is a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 116.37,
          "en": "Though it's a WritableSignal as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.37,
          "end": 118.11,
          "en": "and that might be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.11,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "There's nothing wrong with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "but you also might prefer to expose read only signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 126.78,
          "en": "to your components and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.78,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "So that the only logic that may change the signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 132.93,
          "en": "resides in the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.93,
          "end": 135.51,
          "en": "This is not something you have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.51,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "but something that you could consider doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "so that you enforce a clear separation of the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 143.64,
          "en": "where you manage your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 147.21,
          "en": "and the place where you use that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.21,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "Right now, you could manipulate the data from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.67000000000002,
          "en": "inside the tasks list component since it has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.67000000000002,
          "end": 155.883,
          "en": "to that WritableSignal, and you might not want that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 161.49,
          "en": "Therefore, here in this case, I will go to the tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.49,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "and actually make this tasks signal here private,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "which then in this case means that it can only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "from inside this tasks service class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 176.34300000000002,
          "en": "but not from inside the components that inject the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.66,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "Now, to still expose data, I'll therefore add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.213,
          "en": "a new property, which I'll name allTasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 188.073,
          "en": "which is simply this tasks as read only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 191.61,
          "en": "which is a method offered by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "which in the end also yields a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 196.203,
          "en": "but a read only signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 201.21,
          "en": "And with that back in the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.21,
          "end": 205.02,
          "en": "I can now access allTasks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.02,
          "end": 207.993,
          "en": "And now, tasks is that read only signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "And that makes sure that I can't accidentally change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "that tasks data from inside the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 219.963,
          "en": "and I instead enforce that clear separation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "Now, since tasks is a signal, we should go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 228.39,
          "en": "to the tasks list component, HTML file to the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.39,
          "end": 231.453,
          "en": "and there, read tasks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 234.87,
          "en": "Since it is a signal, we need to read it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.87,
          "end": 238.14,
          "en": "So that Angular also sets up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "behind the scenes, and I want to track the task ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 246.993,
          "en": "as a unique identifier for the individual task items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.78,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "And with that, finally, we got the tasks service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "which manages the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "and has the logic for changing that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 261.93,
          "en": "And we have the new task component, which calls add task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 261.93,
          "end": 265.68,
          "en": "to trigger that method where a new task is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 267.99,
          "en": "as well as the tasks list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.99,
          "end": 270.3,
          "en": "where we also inject the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 273.093,
          "en": "to get hold of those tasks and output them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.96,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "And therefore, with all that done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 280.58,
          "en": "if you save all these files, if you go back to your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.71,
          "end": 284.457,
          "en": "and you add a new task like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.4,
          "end": 290.553,
          "en": "you should see it show up in the tasks list down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.96,
          "end": 294.39,
          "en": "At the moment, changing the status doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.39,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "and this filter doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 298.8,
          "en": "So that's all something we have yet to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.8,
          "end": 303.48,
          "en": "But adding tasks that does work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.48,
          "end": 305.19,
          "en": "and that's of course an important step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.19,
          "end": 308.04,
          "en": "in the right direction and even more importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.04,
          "end": 312.33,
          "en": "allowed us to refresh the important essentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 312.33,
          "end": 316.98,
          "en": "you must know about services and dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.98,
          "end": 320.34,
          "en": "Now, we can continue refining this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.34,
          "end": 323.88,
          "en": "and we can then also dive deeper into services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.88,
          "end": 325.503,
          "en": "and dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
